This study investigates the semileptonic decays of doubly charmed baryons, specifically $\Xi_{cc}^{++} 	o \Xi_{L}^{*} \ell  ar{
u}_{\ell}$ and $\Omega_{cc}^{+} 	o \Omega_{L}^{*} \ell  ar{
u}_{\ell}$, employing a pouch model. The analysis determines the relevant hadronic form factors and calculates the corresponding decay rates. The findings indicate that the semileptonic decay of $\Xi_{L}^{*} \ell  ar{
u}_{\ell}$ is the most prominent among the examined processes, followed by $\Omega_{L}^{*} \ell  ar{
u}_{\ell}$ and $\Omega_{L}^{*} \ell  ar{
u}_{\ell}$. These results are expected to be valuable for future experimental searches.
